  "description": "One exact hologram, many views, for .NET. The Pleroma stores items (a key plus optional flag word, arrangement and time tick) in one fixed array of finite-field harmonics and answers exact counts per key and whole items, refusing past capacity instead of answering wrongly, plus exact counts per flag word, Hamming near-counts and nearest words, counts per arrangement and per tick, opt-in joint counts over flags, order and time, and the count of items whose flag word satisfies any predicate (one read, per tick or arrangement too), all at any load. The whole store relabels flags and arrangements, shifts keys, ages and diffuses over time in place, with every view still exact; several primes per cell and an optional fading complex component are supported. At equal storage against Plate's HRR it recovered 16x the items exactly and gave 0% wrong answers past capacity. CycleHologram is the keys-only special case (exact multiset, replica reconciliation by subtracting holograms). Beneath both, the phasor Vector Symbolic Architecture (VSA) codec: bind, unbind, bundle and correlate over unit-complex faces, with a frozen-identity codec for models and a width-configurable SIMD codec for storage and similarity search.",
